  "title": "A discrete iteration related to Pierce expansions",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Let $a > b > 0$ be integers. Set $b_1 = b$ and $b_{i+1} = {a \\bmod {b_i}}$ for $i \\geq 0$. Eventually we have $b_{n+1} = 0$; put $P(a,b) = n$.\n\nExample: $P(35, 22) = 7$, since $b_1 = 22$, $b_2 = 13$, $b_3 = 9$, $b_4 = 8$, $b_5 = 3$, $b_6 = 2$, $b_7 = 1$, $b_8 = 0$.\n\nProve or disprove: $P(a,b) = O((\\log a)^2)$.",
    "sha256": "fb8d7964f856ae94c7d0d882fa2e1dc78ae2a51d131b7df9f175a788be8ef6e0",
